# headset-build17.env - the feature switches of VR build 17 (build 16's 136 + 34: the bow's nock zone/no-arrow cue/reticle, the hands' size, the vision ramps, the drop's mark, the climb's hug/stand/top-out/head-in-rock and the body follow, the bite/hit sounds/blood, the stagger cap, the hold of Talion, the red warning/dodge/block rule/keep-sword, the gaze strike, the artifact inspect view/hints/text buttons/menu pitch; new blocks at the
# helper). Made from headset-build16.env on 2026-10-27 08:45 (the coordinator); build 16's own file is unchanged (frozen
# in logs/build-vr16/headset.env). At the freeze the coordinator copies it to logs/build-vr17/headset.env.
# scripts/som-vr-headset.sh
# reads that file (KEY=VALUE, one per line; only SOMVR_* keys; read and checked, never executed; see its header).
# The launcher adds its own keys itself: VK_LAYER_PATH, VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS, XR_RUNTIME_JSON (WiVRn), SOMVR_XR_LOG,
# SOMVR_SETTINGS (the user's menu settings file), SOMVR_TUNE. A headset.env next to the build also switches the launch
# to build 6's (no pre-game window, no distro box, scripts/cmds/somvr-vr6.cmd).
# Base: build 5d's set (scripts/som-vr-headset.sh's built-in list) without SOMVR_VIGNETTE=0 (the mod's 0.5 default:
# the user asked for a vignette); then build 6's helpers (logs/boot-check-20261023-155239, the merge boot without
# SOMVR_BODY=hands, which still shows Talion's head and body in the eyes).

# the pipeline, the view, the controls (build 5d)
SOMVR_STEREO=B
SOMVR_VIEWS=xr
SOMVR_COMFORT=1
SOMVR_XR=1
SOMVR_XR_DUMP=600
SOMVR_EYE_SIZE=xr
SOMVR_INPUT=1
SOMVR_POINTER=1
SOMVR_HUD=quad
SOMVR_AUDIO=head
SOMVR_BASE=head
SOMVR_HIDE_HEAD=parts
SOMVR_HEAD_PARTS=main
SOMVR_FALLBACK=auto
SOMVR_ARMS=1
SOMVR_ARMS_STRETCH=1
SOMVR_COMBAT=1
SOMVR_BLADE=controller
SOMVR_VRMENU=1
SOMVR_XR_ENV=on
SOMVR_ANCHOR=root
SOMVR_LOCO=1
SOMVR_LOCO_HOLD=attack
SOMVR_GAMEMOVES=off
SOMVR_COMBAT_REACT=1
SOMVR_CLIMB=b
SOMVR_THREAT=1
SOMVR_BODYMOMENTS=1
SOMVR_SLOTS=1
SOMVR_SLOTS_KEEP=attach
SOMVR_DEFENCE=1
SOMVR_PRACTICE=auto
SOMVR_PRACTICE_AT=32500,2100,-24800

# build 6: bug marks (hold B + Y, or the menu's Report) and the menu's Quit game (handoff/HANDOFF-launch.md)
SOMVR_MARK=1
SOMVR_QUIT=1
# the voice memo: 11 s asked = about 9.5 s recorded (headless, logs/boot-check-20261023-160221: parecord's start and the
# source's wake-up took 1.5 s of 9)
SOMVR_MARK_VOICE_S=11
# build 6: no boot movies (the game's own no-splash byte for the menu's init; logs/boot-check-20261023-165133: the main
# menu at +31 s instead of +55 s, the meadow at +90 s instead of +110 s; docs/re-launcher.md 8)
SOMVR_SKIP_SPLASH=1
# build 6: the sword in two hands (handoff/HANDOFF-hands.md); SOMVR_BODY=hands stays off for now
SOMVR_TWOHAND=1
# build 6: menus in front, the wrist minimap, the controls card, touch (handoff/HANDOFF-menus.md)
SOMVR_XR_MENU=front
SOMVR_XR_MINIMAP=wrist
SOMVR_MINIMAP=head
SOMVR_XR_CARD=on
SOMVR_XR_TOUCH=on
# the hands-only body (build 6 hands round 2, NOTES 17:05): Talion drawn again, everything but the hands folded away
SOMVR_BODY=hands
# build 7 (2026-10-24): the fingers on the controllers (grip = middle/ring/pinky, trigger = index, thumb on a touch; a
# held sword, dagger or hilt = a fist; handoff/HANDOFF-hands.md round 3; the Sword angle row in the wrist menu needs no
# switch); the sword fight (handoff/HANDOFF-combat.md): a parry = the orc's recoil, never the game's counter (the
# counter shows Talion's own back for 2-3 s, then moves the view 55-120 cm: the user's comfort rules)
SOMVR_FINGERS=1
SOMVR_DEFENCE_PARRY=recoil
# build 8 (2026-10-24): the HUD (handoff/HANDOFF-hud.md): the hit streak and the target panel join the minimap on the
# wrist watch; the prompts, hints, XP and place banners in one band 1.3 m ahead, 15 deg below the eyes (0.9 deg per
# 18-px line instead of 0.42). The parry's clank (handoff/HANDOFF-combat.md round 2): the orc's recoil picked from the
# parry/block/hit types, a 120 ms stop, a haptic crack, the game's spark (not seen yet); not `late` (never took).
# Defaults since build 8, no switch: the glance one tick per touch, the hit blade 100 cm (the model's tip), our hits'
# attack type (the orcs' blocks count).
SOMVR_XR_WRIST_HUD=on
SOMVR_XR_PROMPTS=on
SOMVR_DEFENCE_CLANK=recoil,stop,haptic,fx
# build 9 (2026-10-24): climbing works (handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md, re-xr-pipeline.md 32): SOMVR_CLIMB=b's new defaults
# need no line here (SOMVR_CLIMB_SURF=walls, SOMVR_CLIMB_TOP=push with the edge step SOMVR_CLIMB_RAMP=1,
# SOMVR_CLIMB_LOW_CM=50, SOMVR_CLIMB_FIGHT=hold); never SOMVR_CLIMB_TOP=lift|cmd or SOMVR_CLIMB_SURF=any.
# ---- build 10 (2026-10-24 evening, the user's build 9 session's 21 marks; handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md, -combat.md round 3,
# -comfort.md build 10, -vrhands.md, -scale.md; re-xr-pipeline.md 32.7-32.11, 30.12-30.19, 33, 34, 35)
# climbing: both hands open = Talion stays on the wall (A drops); the game's narrow-ledge mode off (the wall-top drift)
SOMVR_CLIMB_LETGO=hang
SOMVR_CLIMB_LEDGES=off
# comfort, sound, prompts: the vignette fitted to the lens; the music at 30 % (the VR menu's Music row); the flat game's
# combat hints dropped; Y held = the wraith vision
SOMVR_VIGNETTE_FIT=lens
SOMVR_MUSIC=0.3
SOMVR_HINTS=off
SOMVR_VISION=hold
# combat: the game's own draws refused (the sword stays on the back); the hands held to the controllers through a draw;
# the hit on Talion felt and seen (a pulse, a red edge); a block = the orc's weapon on the blade in its last 250 ms; the
# light stagger instead of the knockdowns
SOMVR_SLOTS_GAMEDRAW=refuse
SOMVR_ARMS_LW=held
SOMVR_HURT=1
SOMVR_DEFENCE_JUDGE=contact
SOMVR_COMBAT_KNOCKBACK=stagger
# our own hands (the WebXR generic hand, MIT), the watch flat on the back of the left wrist, the wrist menu off the palm
SOMVR_VRHANDS=1
SOMVR_XR_WATCH=wrist
SOMVR_XR_PANEL=palm
# the player size (the VR menu's Player size row, 100-140 % by 5, a blink at each change): 100 % as build 9 until the
# user picks one; at a bigger size the hands and the sword keep the player's own size
SOMVR_PLAYER_SIZE=100
SOMVR_SIZE_BODY=1
# build 11: the bow (the left trigger forms it; the right grip at the string nocks, pull, let go): the release shoots
# at once, the wraith body not drawn over our hands, the string on the string hand, the bow held upright
SOMVR_BOW=1
SOMVR_BOW_RELEASE=now
SOMVR_BOW_GHOST=nomat
SOMVR_BOW_STRING_POS=hand
# SOMVR_BOW_HOLD=auto (builds 11-15b: the bow flat along the arm in a real fist) - build 16: =fist in the bow16 block below
# build 11 bow round 2: the flat pad's prompts for commands no VR control sends hidden (Distract, Focus, Shadow Strike);
# the arrow aims at the head or chest nearest the bow line within 5 deg, else straight (no Shadow Strike while the bow
# is out in build 11: SOMVR_BOW_STRIKE=block, the default; build 12 below: dash)
SOMVR_PAD_PROMPTS=vr
SOMVR_BOW_ASSIST_DEG=5
# build 11: the world hides our hands where they go into it (the game's depth per eye)
SOMVR_XR_HANDS_DEPTH=world
# build 11: a killed orc drops where he stands (no death animation's 3-4 m slide); a block needs the sword hand to
# have moved 15 cm since the strike began (a sword held still no longer blocks)
SOMVR_COMBAT_DEATH=Block_Light
SOMVR_DEFENCE_CONTACT_MOVE_CM=15
# build 11: Celebrimbor's wraith (4 models on Talion's skeleton, seen in cover and while aiming the bow) hidden in the
# eyes while our VR hands replace the body; shadows keep it (handoff/HANDOFF-ghost.md)
SOMVR_HP_POSE=on
# ---- build 12 (2026-10-25, the wraith rounds and the execution; handoff/HANDOFF-wraith.md, -execute.md, -build12.md)
# the bow: X with the bow aimed at an orc = the game's Shadow Strike (when it shows its prompt, 2 arrows a strike); the
# view holds through the lunge, then a 0.3 s dash to the orc under a white-blue tunnel (no blink of the game's)
SOMVR_BOW_STRIKE=dash
# the wraith's wisps on our left hand (the hidden game hand turned and put on our wrist; the bow stays on the grip)
SOMVR_WISPS=hand
# a frame held away from Talion's body (the strike, a body moment's hold): all of him hidden, our arms on the
# controllers, our VR hands and the bow drawn
SOMVR_HP_AWAY=hands
# the execution: 8 hits without a 3 s gap = the game's charge (Urfael glows blue-white, one pulse); the right trigger
# held + a heavy hit = the game's instant kill (0.3x for 0.5 s, some records take the head); the defaults ride with it
# (SOMVR_EXECUTE_GLOW=game, _SEVER=key, _SLOWMO=0.3, _SLOWMO_MS=500, _DEATH=combat)
SOMVR_EXECUTE=1
# the execution's window for a VR player (round 2, handoff/HANDOFF-execute.md; the user's 10 s): the streak - and a full
# charge with it - lapses 10 s after the last hit instead of the game's 3 s (the game's own hit-counter timer, given a
# longer delay while the streak is up: you walk in with the stick, aim and swing for real; still 8 hits, and the orc's
# hits on you still reset it, as in the flat game)
SOMVR_EXECUTE_LAPSE_S=10
SOMVR_EXECUTE_READY_S=10
# the HUD's 3D flourishes (handoff/HANDOFF-hud.md, round 2): the hit streak's blue-white flare and the XP bar's cyan line
# were the game's UI FX drawn in the 3D world, head-locked at the far left of both eyes; not made in play now (the
# streak's `x N` stays on the wrist watch, the XP gains in the band; menus and flat frames keep theirs)
SOMVR_HUD_FX=hide
# ---- build 13 candidates: never a void (HG-9; handoff/HANDOFF-void.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 36). The layer logs every
# gap of 100 ms or more between the game's presents without a switch (`xr: gap N`, SOMVR_XR_GAPS).
# the keep-alive: when the game stops presenting for 100 ms (a hitch, a load that stalls), the layer ends frames of its
# own at the headset's pace with live head tracking - the world's last frame held where it was (the runtime reprojects
# it) over the sky, or the sky and the last board - so the view never freezes to the head
SOMVR_XR_KEEPALIVE=on
# the loading space (needs SOMVR_XR_ENV=on): a stone floor under the sky at the real floor, our hands in every menu and
# load (from the controllers), a loading screen on a calm panel 2.4 m wide 2.4 m ahead (not the 0.6 m touch board) with
# the ember progress lights low ahead through the whole load and any stall; a stall in the world of 1 s fades to the
# space (not a frozen world through a load) and back through the fade
SOMVR_XR_LOADSPACE=on
# a stall is not a menu: a gap of 250 ms between the game's input ticks does not count toward the eye size's 2 s hold
# (without it a world stall over 2 s costs two mode sets after it: 1.6 s of flat, slow frames, boot 221150)
SOMVR_EYE_SIZE_STALL_MS=250
# the theatre: a video's flat frames (the story cutscenes) on a 5 m screen 5 m ahead, SOMVR_BODYMOMENTS' window (in-engine
# cinematics, captain presentations) on 3 m at 3 m, world-locked at eye height where the head faced, in the loading
# space; menus and loading screens keep the board. NOT SEEN AT RUNTIME YET (no video or window in a headless boot so far):
# the mock scenario only; the preload's somvr_session (SOMVR_MARK or SOMVR_QUIT) carries the word
SOMVR_XR_THEATRE=on
# ---- build 13 candidates (2026-10-25 night; the build 12 file grows into build 13's: one line per helper's round)
# the real-game drill (handoff/HANDOFF-drill.md): the practice's Go / Back asked for in the pause menu (the wrist menu
# opens there), at the Nemesis board after a death or in a scripted moment waits until the game is back for 1 s, the
# menu's buttons busy meanwhile (build 12: at once - its black hid the pause menu until the player unpaused blind; at
# the board its teleport landed in the respawn and left the game's black loading cover in front for 40-60 s)
SOMVR_PRACTICE_WAIT=1
# ---- build 13 candidate (2026-10-25, the user's climbing idea: "Gorilla tag inspired ... just let me sling myself up";
# handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md, re-xr-pipeline.md 32.14): let go of the wall while the hand still pulls fast = Talion flies
# on up the wall (only up, a little sideways: never away from the wall or down), catches a higher hold with a grip, or
# hangs where the throw tops out (no fall); a slow let-go hangs as before, A drops. Tunables (defaults):
# SOMVR_CLIMB_FLING_MIN=150 (cm/s up), _GAIN=1, _MAX=500 (cm/s), _SIDE=0.5, _G=981 (cm/s^2), _WIN_MS=100
SOMVR_CLIMB_FLING=on
# build 13, hands that stop at surfaces (docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 38, handoff/HANDOFF-surfaces.md; the HL:A gap HG-6):
# the hand you see and the sword in it stop at stone, wood and the ground (the game's own rays from the shoulder to the
# palm, the palm to the finger tips, along the blade); the IK arm, the drawn sword and the combat's blade follow the
# stopped hand, a faint wraith-blue ghost of the real hand shows once the two part by 4 cm; a tick at a hand's contact,
# the clank (and the defence's sparks when fast) at the blade's. Orcs' bodies never stop a hand or the blade (the hits
# land as before); never clamped: a climb's holding hand, the bow, the wrist panel, a pause, a finisher
SOMVR_HANDS_SURFACE=on
# never a void, round 2 (handoff/HANDOFF-void.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 36.7-36.8): the game's in-world loading cover -
# after every fast travel (4-6 s) and a far respawn (40-60 s) the game puts opaque black with a spinner on its UI while
# the world goes on; build 12 showed it as a black slab with holes 1.5 m ahead. The layer reads a 16 x 9 grid of the HUD
# image each frame: the HUD, the band and the wrist minimap go as soon as it turns dark, and a cover held 300 ms
# (SOMVR_XR_COVER_MS) is a load - the world fades to the loading space with the ember progress lights and our hands, and
# back through the fade when the game lifts the cover (needs SOMVR_XR_ENV; the floor and the lights SOMVR_XR_LOADSPACE)
SOMVR_XR_COVER=on
# the in-world menus' backdrop: the pause menu, the map and their pages on the board over the live world get a dark
# panel behind the board (6 cm larger on each side, a soft rim) and the world dimmed 40 % (SOMVR_XR_MENU_BACK_DIM)
# behind it, rising over 0.12 s at the open (the drill's finding 4: Options unreadable over a forge tower's white marble)
SOMVR_XR_MENU_BACK=on
# ---- build 13 candidates (2026-10-26, the Nemesis verbs; handoff/HANDOFF-verbs.md, re-xr-pipeline.md 39)
# the left hand = the wraith hand, the game decides every outcome: reach to an orc's head or collar (or reach the arm out
# at it) and squeeze = the game's grab, held while the grip is closed, opened = let go; holding it, the left trigger =
# the drain (the brand where the game has it unlocked; this save: "NoBrand"); holding it, pull the orc to your face =
# the interrogation, then the trigger = Interrogate (the game's intel menu) or the sword into it = Eliminate; the sword
# into a held orc = the grab's own move; the trigger with the open hand on an orc's head = a tap the stun, held the
# combat drain; the sword on an orc the game offers its silent stealth kill for = that kill. The game's grab and
# interrogation are held first person (the body moments' hold, the view eased 35 cm back from the held orc's head);
# their prompts stay in the band with the game's words, their letters the Touch's that do the same (holding: X = the
# grab's move, A = the interrogation; its choice: B = Eliminate; the drain and Interrogate shown as LT, the left
# trigger); the bow does not take the left trigger meanwhile
SOMVR_VERBS=on
# build 13 candidate (2026-10-26, the verbs' glow; handoff/HANDOFF-verbs.md, re-xr-pipeline.md 39.7): the interrogation's
# pull brought the game's wraith flare on Talion's left hand (its FX domination_in / domination_loop) to ~25 cm from the
# eyes: a white-blue burst filling the middle of both eyes. hide = those two FX are not made while the game draws our
# eyes; the orc's own wraith glow (domination_brand_*), the wraith world and the drains' glow stay (the wraith at work).
# game = as built (the flare); SOMVR_VERBS_GLOW_FX=WORD,WORD names other FX to leave out
SOMVR_VERBS_GLOW=hide
# ---- build 13 candidate (2026-10-26, the drill's finding 1: a forge tower top had no way down; handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md,
# re-xr-pipeline.md 40): at an edge, reach over it and grip its lip (or the wall just under it): the climb starts from
# the top; push the hand up: Talion goes out over the edge and down the face, then hand over hand down (a hold pushed up
# lowers him, as climbing up); a light tick in the hand = the lip can be gripped. A while hanging (or holding the lip on
# the top) with the ground more than 4 m under his feet = a blink to it (the practice trip's fade: black, he stands
# there, back); lower = the real fall (no fall damage in this game); no ground under him or water = A does nothing (a
# double buzz). Tunables (defaults): SOMVR_CLIMB_BLINK_CM=400 (the blink from this high), SOMVR_CLIMB_LIP_DROP_CM=150
# (a lip: the ground beyond it this far under it), SOMVR_CLIMB_BLINK_MAX_CM=8000
SOMVR_CLIMB_DESCENT=on
# build 13 candidate (2026-10-26, HG-11: crouch by ducking; handoff/HANDOFF-crouch.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 41): the
# player ducks for real (the head 28 cm below its height at the recentre for 0.15 s) and Talion goes into the game's
# stealth crouch (CombatSecondary04 held = PC_Stealth, the dagger); standing up (back above 18 cm below for 0.2 s, at
# least 0.5 s down) stands him up. The view drops by the real duck only (the root anchor: the game's crouch never moves
# it). The right stick down toggles the crouch (seated play keeps only that; the stock Crouch it sent in build 12 never
# did anything). A short pulse on both hands when he is down; the crouched walk at most 150 cm/s (SOMVR_CROUCH_CMS).
# The VR menu's Crouch row: Duck / Button. Tunables: SOMVR_CROUCH_DEPTH_CM, _UP_CM, _ON_MS, _OFF_MS, _HOLD_MS, _HAPTIC
SOMVR_CROUCH=duck
# ---- build 14 candidate (2026-10-26, HG-5: front-first enemies; handoff/HANDOFF-front.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 42):
# the fight circle (the game's turn-taking) may no longer give an orc behind the player (out of the headset's 110 deg
# view) its attack at once: first it is warned for 1 s (the warning sound at that orc, the edge glow on its side
# rising, one pulse on that side's hand: a THREAT "pre" warning), then it may attack; orcs in view attack as before.
# Off = the flat game's choice (any orc of the circle, from behind too). log = the hooks only (logs, nothing changed).
# Tunables (defaults): SOMVR_FRONT_WARN_S=1.0, _READY_S=2.0, _QUIET_S=2.0, _VIEW_DEG=110 (THREAT's), _FAR_M=0 (all),
# _MAX_WARN=1. Off by default in the mod; on here
SOMVR_FRONT=1
# the AI's camera copy from the head (the game's "on screen" for the attacker score, the attacks that want their
# attacker on or off screen, the ambient spawner's off-screen spawns and the off-screen despawns): head = where the
# player looks (the headset's 110 x 90 deg), off = the flat game's hidden orbit camera (a 37 x 40 deg cone that swings on
# its own). head: the game itself then prefers the orcs in view, and spawns/despawns stay out of view (run 085304: none
# in view; with off, run 084439: 3 of 6 in the player's view; re-xr-pipeline.md 42.10)
SOMVR_FRONT_CAMCOPY=head
# the slot's lockout between two attacks x this (the game's 0.25 s re-arm, 0.75 s disarm): 1 = the game's
SOMVR_FRONT_LOCKOUT=1.0
# the attack damage at Talion x this (D10: 0.5 = half; amounts from 1000 on stay: scripted kills): 1 = the game's
SOMVR_FRONT_DAMAGE=1.0
# ---- build 14 candidate, front-first round 2 (2026-10-26, the threat14 helper; handoff/HANDOFF-front.md "Round 2",
# docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 42.11): THREAT's in-view test = FRONT's: the orc's bearing off the head (|yaw|), the pitch
# ignored (a close orc at Talion's feet is 50-77 deg below the eyes and seen: no more LATE edge warnings for it);
# full = round 1's full angle off the view direction (FRONT follows: one test)
SOMVR_THREAT_VIEW=bearing
# one warning per attack from out of view: FRONT's warning (the sound at the orc, one pulse on its side, the edge glow
# rising) is that attack's only sound and pulse; THREAT skips its own announce, sound and urgent pulse for it, and the
# edge glow stays on from the warning to the blow. 0 = round 1's (3 pulses and 2 sounds per blow from behind)
SOMVR_FRONT_ONECUE=1
# THREAT: an orc's "attack" with no key at all (no impact, no parry window, no hit frame, no shot) gets no cue: those are
# the orcs' moves between blows (run 092140, five orcs: 200 of 254 attack starts, none a blow, 114 of 148 out-of-view
# pulses and sounds). 1 = round 1's (a pulse and the sound for each of them out of view: a buzz storm in a crowd)
SOMVR_THREAT_KEYLESS=0
# build 14 candidate (2026-10-26, the story drill: handoff/HANDOFF-story.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 43): B does what the
# flat pad's RB does at a story moment. A pick prompt ('Combat_Activate_*': an herb's "Restore Health", arrows; the game
# puts them on CombatSecondary02 123, which B never sent and the prompt band dropped) is shown with B's glyph and B
# picks; at a mission's marker B = "(RB) Start Mission" (QuestConfirm 282); while a presentation or a cinematic is up in
# the world (the mission card "(A) Accept (B) Cancel", a failed mission's "(A) Retry (B) Abandon") A, B, X, Y and the
# grips are the pad's buttons for the quest and skip commands only, each when the game has it active (a button held
# when the window opens counts after its release). Never a move, a jump or a combat command; nothing in a menu (the
# pad passthrough there already). Lines: USE ...
SOMVR_USE=1
# build 14 candidate (the story drill): a story video (a mission's start, `video=1`) comes as layout-B presents with no
# eye images, which build 13 answered with the last stereo frame again for the whole video (56 s frozen, the video only
# heard). With this switch they are mono frames: the video on the theatre's 5 m screen 5 m ahead (SOMVR_XR_THEATRE).
SOMVR_XR_THEATRE_VIDEO=on
# build 14 candidate (the story drill): the theatre places each new presentation, video or load again where the head
# faces now (build 13 kept the first window's place for every later window: one could come up behind the player).
SOMVR_XR_THEATRE_RESEAT=on
# ---- the story drill's round 2 (2026-10-26, handoff/HANDOFF-story.md "Round 2", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 43.6-43.9):
# with SOMVR_USE the Controls page says "Use: B (pick, missions)" and keeps "Sprint: click left stick" (the crouch's
# line had pushed it off; the story's first objective is timed and its hint names the sprint): Menu and Pause share a line.
# The theatre's screens (a story video, a presentation: a captain's introduction, a mission card, a failed screen) are
# 1.33 x their distance wide: 4 m at 3 m, 6.65 m at 5 m (67 deg, was 53): a captain's line 0.8 deg instead of 0.6
# (logs/story2-pictures/theatre-size-*.png: the same frame at 3 and 4 m, at a Quest 2's pixel density). 100 = build 13.
SOMVR_XR_THEATRE_SIZE=133
# ---- build 15 candidate: the story's way-finding (2026-10-26, handoff/HANDOFF-objective.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 44):
# the HUD's objective coin was placed by the game's flat 43 x 25 deg camera, so in VR it hugged the HUD quad's edge
# whatever the head did. With this switch the game's own marker (its nav marker 'Objective': the place the game shows)
# is drawn by the layer as a small gold diamond with the distance under it ("236 m"), world-locked over the objective's
# direction (4 deg, its quad at most 12 m away, faint within 5 deg of the view's centre); out of view a gold arrow at
# the view's edge points the way (5 deg, head-locked 1 m ahead). The game's coin is hidden in our stereo frames (the
# game's own hide). Nothing moves, nothing is pressed. SOMVR_OBJECTIVE=both keeps the game's coin too, =off as build 14.
SOMVR_OBJECTIVE=on
# ---- the collect drill (2026-10-26, handoff/HANDOFF-collect.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 45): no new switch. An
# artifact's prompt shows only in the wraith vision near it (the game's rule): hold Y there, "(B) Pick Up" comes in
# 2-3 s (SOMVR_USE above keeps it and shows B), B picks it and opens its menu (A, the right stick, X, B, B, Start).
# Known open: that menu's artifact is not drawn in VR (our eyes stay in the world); Ithildin glyphs are not collected.
# ---- build 15b (the weapons helper, 2026-10-26, handoff/HANDOFF-weapons15b.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 46): build 15's
# headset session lost the sword after the bow: the right stick's stealth crouch (latched during the bow) is PC_Stealth,
# which makes Acharn (slot 1) the active item, so the sword's draw was refused ("another weapon is active", DENIED) and
# Acharn hung in Talion's hidden hand ("my sword is floating in the middle of me"). With this switch the sword's draw
# (the player's or the restore after the bow) stands the stealth crouch up and activates melee first, and an active
# Acharn not in the left hand is not drawn in the eyes while the body is hidden. A kill's Acharn is still left alone.
SOMVR_SLOTS_STEALTH=on
# build 15b: the bow off the left trigger (the session's #6/#7: "when I grab the sword I should be pressing left
# trigger", "especially for climbing"): the bow hangs behind the left shoulder; the left grip pressed there brings it
# out and holds it while closed, let go there puts it back (let go elsewhere: the hands apart end it, as before). The
# string grip at the nock brings no bow any more. The left trigger counts as a grab (the climb's holds, the sword's
# hilt with both hands). The Controls page: "Bow: L grip at L shoulder". SOMVR_BOW_DRAW=trigger = build 15's.
SOMVR_BOW_DRAW=slot
# ---- build 15b candidate: smoother hands, a weighted sword (2026-10-26, handoff/HANDOFF-feel.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md
# 48). The user after build 15: the hands "a bit jittery ... mainly when holding the sword" and "add some 'weight' to
# the sword". No pipeline cause (the grips at the eyes' own time, the held sword not moved by the game); the shake is
# the controller's own, made visible by the 1 m blade. SOMVR_HANDS_SMOOTH=on: an adaptive (One Euro) filter on the grips,
# steady at rest (~2 Hz), no delay in a swing (4 ms at 172 deg/s, 1.3 ms at 573 deg/s); the drawn sword = the hits'
# blade. SOMVR_SWORD_WEIGHT=light: in fast swings only, the blade trails up to 3 deg and settles (heavy: 6 deg), a soft
# pulse on a fast swing, fuller hits; still or slow hands get nothing. Off: SOMVR_HANDS_SMOOTH=off / SOMVR_SWORD_WEIGHT=off.
# HANDJIT lines (every 10 s) measure the shake at the hand and the 1 m tip, raw and smoothed.
SOMVR_HANDS_SMOOTH=on
# (SOMVR_SWORD_WEIGHT: build 16 sets it in the sword16 block at the end)
# ---- build 15b, the loading voices (2026-10-26, handoff/HANDOFF-loadvoices.md, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 47): session
# 165456 mark 11 "The voices I hear in the loading screen are kind of weird ... You might just want to turn them off".
# Through a load on flat frames the game's dialogue volume (its RTPC options_dialog) is sent as 0 and its own value
# back after the load; music and sound effects untouched. The game's voices in loads again: SOMVR_LOAD_VOICES=game.
SOMVR_LOAD_VOICES=off
# build 15b, the lip (handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md "build 15b", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 47.2): session 165456 mark 8,
# stuck under a slab sticking out over the face. A pull the game blocks under a hold over the eyes goes out round the
# lip (at most 40 cm, SOMVR_CLIMB_OVERHANG_CM); a hold 50+ cm over a reached top forgets it; pulls held 0.4 s under a
# found top = descent's blink onto it. Off: SOMVR_CLIMB_OVERHANG=off.
# The coordinator, 10-26 18:30: off for 15b - proven in 1 of 2 boots, and its automatic blink onto the top breaks
# the user's rule for ability moves (a clear when, a known where, a cancel); on again once it's player-triggered.
SOMVR_CLIMB_OVERHANG=off
# build 16, the quit (the quit16 helper; docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 53, handoff/HANDOFF-launch.md "build 16"): 15b crashed
# at every exit() (the menus' Quit game, boot_check's SIGTERM) - the keep-alive called the runtime after the OpenXR
# loader unloaded it, Feral's crash reporter kept the game alive. At the exit our threads stop first (an exit handler),
# the hooks pass through, the runtime's library is pinned. Default on; off = build 15b.
SOMVR_XR_EXIT=on
# build 15b's follow-up (the weapons helper, after the 15b freeze; re-xr-pipeline.md 46.5): marks #4/#5 "they're not
# holding it right": the fist closed at the crossguard, the leather grip out behind it. The drawn sword slides 8 cm ahead
# along its blade in the right fist (the right weapon node's calibration, before the sword angle), so the fist closes on
# the leather right under the guard; the combat blade's tip 8 cm farther with it (what you see is what hits). The two
# hands' grab is unchanged (the left hand 8..24 cm behind the right grip: on the leather toward the pommel). 0 = build 15.
SOMVR_SWORD_GRIP_CM=8
# ---- build 16, the sword's weight (the sword16 helper; docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 52, handoff/HANDOFF-feel.md "build 16"):
# session 233334 mark 6: the sword needs more weight (light's trail let it be wiggled freely with one hand). Heavy
# (Blade & Sorcery's feel): one hand, the blade's direction follows the hand through an acceleration limit - slow cuts 1:1, fast cuts trail 11-16 deg and catch up in 0.1-0.3 s, a quick 5 Hz wiggle moves the blade a third as much;
# the twist and the hand stay 1:1; both hands on the hilt near 1:1; a drag pulse, fuller hits. The VR menu's Sword weight
# row (Off / Light / Heavy) changes it live. Build 15b's: light (its 3-degree trail). Off: SOMVR_SWORD_WEIGHT=off.
SOMVR_SWORD_WEIGHT=heavy
# build 16 (the sword16 helper): the right grip each frame the weight applies into <somvr.log>.swordrec (text, ~5 KB/s
# while the sword is drawn, at most 48 MB) - the user's own swings and wiggles, replayed offline through every weight
# level (tests/test_smooth.c SWG_REPLAY=FILE) to tune the next build. Off: SOMVR_SWORD_REC=off.
SOMVR_SWORD_REC=on
# build 16 (the sword16 helper): the drawn hands with the weighted blade - fixed (the hands stay on the controllers, the
# handle turns in the fist by up to 16 deg in a fast heavy cut) or follow (the layer's hands turn with the blade about
# their grips, the fist stays closed on it; positions and the twist stay 1:1). Fixed: never laggy hands.
SOMVR_SWORD_WEIGHT_HAND=fixed
# ---- build 16: the wraith round (the wraith16 helper, 2026-10-27; handoff/HANDOFF-wraith.md "build 16", docs/
# re-xr-pipeline.md 49). Y and the wraith vision (SOMVR_VISION=hold above) is fixed in the code: a press with the vision
# on turns it off, Y not held while it is ours turns it off, the taps wait out the game's ~1 s dwell. The weapons' glowing
# wraith copies: the ones of a weapon hidden in the eyes (the sheathed sword, the dagger, in the vision and the bow's aim)
# are hidden too; the held weapon's glow stays. Off: SOMVR_HP_COPIES=off (build 15b).
SOMVR_HP_COPIES=on
# ---- build 16, the bow (the bow16 helper, 2026-10-27, handoff/HANDOFF-bow.md "build 16", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 51):
# session 233334 mark 1, the bow lay flat along the arm: builds 11-15b laid its shot on the grip's +Z, the fist's tube -
# up for a real bow hold (that session's idle ray (-0.087 0.981 0.176)). HOLD=fist: the limbs along the fist, the shot
# along the arm, the string toward the face, the bow's own grip in the hand (this line replaces SOMVR_BOW_HOLD=auto above;
# the later line wins). The string on the right trigger: RT at the string nocks, pull with it held, let go of RT = the
# shot. The quiver: RT behind the right shoulder (the sword's place; the sword's grip there only while the bow is away)
# takes an arrow (seen in the hand, drawn by the layer); touched to the string it is nocked; let go before that it is
# gone; let go below 20 cm of draw it rests on the string; none left = nothing and a buzz. The Controls page: "Arrow: RT
# at R shoulder", "Shoot: nock, pull, let go". Our shot's arrow is ImmediateImpact (never drawn): the layer draws it
# flying on at 70 m/s (SOMVR_BOW_FLIGHT_MPS, the default). Our shot had no sound (the stock one comes with its
# animation): the stock shot's own events, found with SOMVR_BOW_SNDLOG - the draw's creak at the nock (cut at the
# release) and the bow's fire at the release, from the bow hand. Back to build 15b's: HOLD=auto, STRING=grip,
# QUIVER=off, SOUND and DRAW_SOUND off.
SOMVR_BOW_HOLD=fist
SOMVR_BOW_STRING=trigger
SOMVR_BOW_QUIVER=on
SOMVR_BOW_SOUND=wra_bow_fire_plyr
SOMVR_BOW_DRAW_SOUND=wra_bow_damage_draw
# ---- build 16, the climb16 helper (handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md "build 16", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 50): session 233334
# marks 2/3, pinned at the meadow bank's lip (held as if in a ledge state). UNPIN: Talion's capsule caught in the rock (the proxy's own
# contacts inside a wall), every level move undone: the asked move (the stick's, a pull's; at most 8 cm a tick) given
# to the proxy, never into what he touches or toward a wall. PULLOVER: where the climb is blocked at a top's edge with
# room for him on the top, a ring shows there; that hand pulled 25 cm = a quick blink onto it; opening the hand cancels
# (no room: a soft double buzz). HANG_STICK_CM:
# hanging with the feet at most 60 cm over the ground, the stick = he stands and walks. Off: =off / =0.
SOMVR_CLIMB_UNPIN=on
SOMVR_CLIMB_PULLOVER=on
SOMVR_CLIMB_HANG_STICK_CM=60
# combat16 helper (handoff/HANDOFF-combat.md "build 16", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 54): the infantry's overhead chop lands at
# its sibling strikes' reach and no orc walks into Talion (90 cm from his root); a committed edge-leading cut is the
# game's Medium strike (its High one, the shield breaker, from a hit streak of 8) and a raised shield glances it; a hit
# that would leave an orc 12 health or less kills it (an orc left at a sliver stopped fighting).
SOMVR_FIGHT_REACH=AI_Infantry_Melee_Front_3_LL:65..85
SOMVR_FIGHT_SPACE_CM=90
SOMVR_COMBAT_CLASS=cut
SOMVR_COMBAT_SLIVER=12
# ---- build 16 round 2, the climb2 helper (handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md "build 16 round 2", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 50.8-50.9):
# THROUGH: a pull blocked under a hold over the eyes (the capsule held under a lip it cannot pass) goes up through the
# rock 1:1 with the hand, as the game's own wall run passes it; never with rock at or round the head (rays). Off: =off.
# FACE_TOWARD: a hold taken with the palm or the fingers along the wall uses the wall's own direction (no early "over"
# with the feet still under a top). Off: =off.
SOMVR_CLIMB_THROUGH=on
SOMVR_CLIMB_FACE_TOWARD=on
# The arrow seen is the game's own glowing arrow: it rides Talion's right weapon node while the bow is out (the wraith
# round found it), so that node now follows the quiver - in the hand, nocked, drawn, resting on the string, flying on
# after the shot - and is put away out of sight with no arrow taken (the layer's own arrow only with this off).
SOMVR_BOW_GAME_ARROW=on
# combat16 round 2 (re-xr-pipeline.md 54.8): the space kept from the player's head too (the nearer of the head and
# Talion's root: leaning or stepping in no longer lets an orc into the face); the shield physical, B&S-style: a cut
# whose blade meets the shield (a 40 cm sphere about its model) before the body glances with the clank, one around it
# (low, high, its open side) lands - against a lone shield orc the angle rule left nothing that works in VR.
SOMVR_FIGHT_SPACE_FROM=head
SOMVR_COMBAT_SHIELD=physical
SOMVR_COMBAT_SHIELD_CM=40
# ---- build 17, the climb17 helper (handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md "build 17: top-outs", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 60):
# HUG: while climbing, a hand pushed toward the wall never shoves him off it (the move away from the face is cut once
# his root is 50 cm from the hold's face); further out a pull takes him back toward it. Off: =off.
# STAND: at a top, a floor under his capsule = letting go stands him on it (and a push that brings his feet onto it
# ends the climb); a topped hang with his capsule's rim on the top: the stick walks him onto it. Off: =off.
# HEAD_ROCK: the head within 8 cm of a surface fades the view, black 2 cm past it; black 0.5 s = the view back at
# Talion's eyes; also at any of our blinks' black (the drift of real steps dropped). =fade: the fade only; =off.
# TOPOUT: at a top with the head over it, a push the game's collision holds at the edge's corner goes through the rock
# 1:1 (the head's way kept clear by rays; the ring stays the fallback). Off: =off.
# FOLLOW (the build-5 body follow, off since build 4b): the session's real steps left the eyes 64-104 cm off Talion's
# root (the orcs aim at the root: every blow landed in front of the player); now his root follows the head's ground
# position once it is 20 cm off, at most 4 cm a frame (3.6 m/s at 90 Hz), with the game's collision; the view does
# not move (the rig's origin takes the move), no body is drawn. Off: SOMVR_FOLLOW=0.
SOMVR_CLIMB_HUG=on
SOMVR_CLIMB_STAND=on
SOMVR_CLIMB_TOPOUT=through
SOMVR_HEAD_ROCK=on
SOMVR_FOLLOW=1
SOMVR_FOLLOW_CM=20
SOMVR_FOLLOW_STEP_CM=4
# ---- build 17, the menu17 helper (docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 56, handoff/HANDOFF-menus.md "build 17"): no new switches.
# The VR menu's Sword hand row (Fixed / Follow = SOMVR_SWORD_WEIGHT_HAND live) and Arrows row (Quiver / Auto =
# SOMVR_BOW_QUIVER live, taken while the bow is away) start from the lines above (fixed, on); the Controls page's lines
# follow them (Block, 2 hands, Dagger, Ledge added; 21 lines). The practice page's Refill arrows + focus and Refill
# health buttons need nothing but SOMVR_PRACTICE (their three read-only calls are byte-checked at start).
# ---- the collectibles (the collect drill's round 2, the inspect16 helper, 2026-10-26/27; handoff/HANDOFF-collect.md
# "Round 2", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 45.7-45.10). SOMVR_INSPECT=on: while the game is paused in a menu whose picture
# comes from a camera of its own (580-600 m under the map: an artifact's inspect view, Sauron's Army's captains, the
# Appendices' walls) those frames render flat from the game's camera on the menu board (the same 0.72 m board, where
# the menu opened; nothing moves with the game's camera): the artifact in front of the player, the sticks turn and zoom
# it, "(X) Play Memory" when its memory point is found, X plays the memory (its voiced verse on the board). Build 16
# showed the world at Talion's head there (the object never seen). The pause menu's own page shows the flat game's
# scene behind its text too. Two mode sets (~150 ms each) at each such menu's start and end. off = build 16.
SOMVR_INSPECT=on
# SOMVR_HINTS=off dropped the game's own collectible tutorial, shown once near an artifact or an Ithildin ("Enter the
# Wraith World (LB) to find the nearby Ithildin." - the pad's glyph; our Y): with this its key's hints pass, the fight's
# button hints stay dropped. Unset = build 16.
SOMVR_HINTS_KEEP=Tut_Collectible_
# The UI texts' button icons (tutorials, hints, tips): the game draws an action's icon from the flat pad's binding, so
# the wraith vision (CombatSecondary01 122) showed LB; in VR it is held on Y: with this its icon is the pad's Y (the
# icon of CombatPrimary02 119) - "Enter the Wraith World (Y) ...". The binding itself is untouched. Unset = build 16.
SOMVR_TEXT_BUTTONS=122:119
# A game menu opened while the head looks down (an artifact's pick at the feet) gets its board down the gaze, at most
# 30 deg below the level (still facing the eyes, where it opened; looking up keeps the level board). 0 = build 16.
SOMVR_XR_MENU_PITCH=30
# ---- build 17, the descent17 helper (handoff/HANDOFF-climb.md "build 17: the drop's marker", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 55):
# A at an edge or on a wall no longer blinks Talion down at once: A held shows where he will land (a gold ring on the
# ground, a faint line from the edge down to it; nowhere safe - no ground, water, an orc there, no room - = no ring and a
# soft double buzz), A let go after 0.3 s goes there under a quick fade (0.42 s nominal), the move stick while A is held
# cancels (and walks only once let go and pushed again), a shorter tap does nothing. Controls page: "Drop: hold A, let
# go". Off: =off (A blinks down at once, as build 16). The hold: SOMVR_CLIMB_DESCENT_MARK_HOLD_MS (default 300).
SOMVR_CLIMB_DESCENT_MARK=on
# bow17 helper (build 17, docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 61): the bow's nock anywhere near the string's middle (25 cm) with the
# draw counted behind it; a double buzz for an empty hand at the string (three knocks: the quiver empty); the game's
# crosshair never shown (the arrow is the aim); our hands 20 % bigger round the sword's and the bow's grips; the wraith
# look's lighting ramps in/out in 0.15 s, not the game's 1 s (the vision record, also the bow's aim).
SOMVR_BOW_NOCK_ZONE=string
SOMVR_BOW_NOARROW_CUE=buzz
SOMVR_BOW_RETICLE=hide
SOMVR_XR_HANDS_SIZE=1.2
SOMVR_VISION_RAMP_MS=150,150
# ---- build 17, the block17 helper (handoff/HANDOFF-combat.md "build 17: blocking", docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 62): the
# build-16 session's "I can't figure out how to block these attacks". Blows DEFENCE never blocks (cannot-block, cannot-
# parry, and now cannot-counter: the defender's spear sweeps, the flat game's red prompt) are told at their wind-up: the
# orc's weapons and body glow red and pulse, out of view the edge is red, three buzzes in both hands then a double just
# before the impact, a warning sound; the way out: step/lean 30 cm aside or 40 cm back, or A = a 1.5 m dodge (the left
# stick's direction, else straight away from the attacker; the wraith tunnel; never into a wall or off a ledge: refused
# with a double buzz; 0.5 s cooldown). A block counts with either the drawn (weighted, trailing) blade or the blade where
# the hand holds it, its centre within 15 cm of the orc's weapon, the guard moved 15 cm (grip or tip). The glows sit on
# the orc's weapons (a berserker's two: the striking one brighter). In a fight with the sword in hand the climb takes no
# new hold (a grip by a wall put the sword away: "my sword clips around"). Off: each switch's =off / the old values.
SOMVR_THREAT_RED=on
SOMVR_THREAT_AT=weapon
SOMVR_DEFENCE_RED_TYPES=parry,counter,block
SOMVR_DEFENCE_CONTACT_BLADE=both
SOMVR_DEFENCE_CONTACT_MOVE_FROM=blade
SOMVR_DEFENCE_CONTACT_CM=15
SOMVR_DEFENCE_KEEP_SWORD=on
SOMVR_DODGE=on
# stagger17 helper (build 17; docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 58): an orc we hit or parry reels back at most this far from where
# the hit found it (1:1 to half of it, then slowing to a stop; a step toward Talion free, FIGHT_SPACE's 90 cm after it)
# instead of =stagger's 1.4-1.9 m and the walk back; 0 = measured only (`COMBAT reel` lines)
SOMVR_COMBAT_STAGGER_CM=55

# build 17, the strike17 helper (docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 63, handoff/HANDOFF-wraith.md "build 17"): the Shadow Strike by
# gaze - in the wraith vision (Y held) the orc the head looks at is marked (a wraith-blue ring round it, "A Shadow
# Strike" beside it; grey "No arrows" under 2 arrows); A = the game's own strike at it with build 12's wraith dash;
# looking away or letting go of Y first = nothing. Needs SOMVR_BOW_STRIKE=dash, SOMVR_BOW=1, SOMVR_VISION=hold (above).
SOMVR_STRIKE_GAZE=on
# ---- build 17, the bite17 helper (docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 59, handoff/HANDOFF-feel.md "build 17: the bite"): a full
# cut that lands bites - the drawn blade stops in the orc where it went in (the hand moves on: the handle turns in the
# fist) for at most 60 ms, or until it is 30 deg off (a fast cut tears free sooner), then eases back onto the hand over
# 100 ms; a full pulse while it bites and a short beat when it comes free (no ring: that is the block's clank). Taps,
# flat slaps and stabs never bite. The VR menu's "Blade bite" row turns it off and on. Off: SOMVR_COMBAT_BITE=off.
SOMVR_COMBAT_BITE=on
SOMVR_COMBAT_BITE_MS=60
SOMVR_COMBAT_BITE_EASE_MS=100
SOMVR_COMBAT_BITE_DEG=30
# Each landed hit kind sounds its own over the game's hit sound (the game's own events, at the contact): a cut a heavy
# body impact, a flat slap a thin knock, a stab the blow-on-a-body thud (a tap as a slap); a cut shows blood and a stab
# sparks at the contact (the game's FX). Off: SOMVR_COMBAT_HITSND=off / SOMVR_COMBAT_HITFX=off.
SOMVR_COMBAT_HITSND=on
SOMVR_COMBAT_HITFX=on
# ---- build 17, the nomove17 helper (handoff/HANDOFF-combat.md "build 17: no game moves of the player",
# docs/re-xr-pipeline.md 64): an enemy's paired sync on Talion (the berserker's headbutt after a Medium hit on it, its
# bodyslam, the defender's wrecker, the throat grab, the captains' counters) plays in place: LOCO keeps his ticks, the
# game's root motion goes (build 16: the headbutt carried him and the view 86 cm); the blow, the damage, the red flash
# and the buzz stay. Off: =off.
SOMVR_COMBAT_HOLD_TALION=on
